<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
findajob.pro — pull the VPS database dumps to the laptop, daily.

Repo copy:   deploy/com.geronimo.findajob-backup-pull.plist
Installed:   ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.geronimo.findajob-backup-pull.plist

  cp deploy/com.geronimo.findajob-backup-pull.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.geronimo.findajob-backup-pull.plist 2>/dev/null
  launchctl load   ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.geronimo.findajob-backup-pull.plist
  launchctl start  com.geronimo.findajob-backup-pull          # run it once now
  tail ~/Library/Logs/findajob-backup-pull.log

07:30 local. The VPS writes its dump at 03:41 in ITS timezone, which is
Etc/UTC — verified with timedatectl, not assumed — and the laptop is EEST
(UTC+3), so the dump lands at 06:41 local. 07:30 leaves an hour of slack for a
slow dump without waiting so long that a whole working day passes first.

A LaunchAgent, not a cron entry: launchd runs a missed StartCalendarInterval
job when the machine next wakes, which is the normal case for a laptop that is
closed at 07:30. cron would simply skip it and say nothing.

The paths are absolute and include this user's home. That is a real limitation
of keeping the file in the repo — if the checkout ever moves, this breaks
silently until the staleness check in the script starts failing, which is
exactly what that check is for.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.geronimo.findajob-backup-pull</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/Geronimo/Projects/findajob/deploy/pull-backups.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>7</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>

    <!-- Not at load: this fires on every login, and a pull that just ran an
         hour ago is noise in the log rather than another copy. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- Appended, never truncated: the whole point of the BACKUP-PULL line is
         being able to ask "when did this last work?" months later. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/Geronimo/Library/Logs/findajob-backup-pull.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/Geronimo/Library/Logs/findajob-backup-pull.log</string>

    <!-- ssh needs a usable PATH; launchd gives an agent almost nothing. -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
